    "evenflo_faq_tCY88x": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_HzmB77": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Where can I find the installation video?",
            "content": "<p>You can find (5) install how-to videos, outlining the install of each car-seat mode on our YouTube Channel <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL2XWgmXQu0adqcQCNeY9fGZMIcAxl2CJd\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL2XWgmXQu0adqcQCNeY9fGZMIcAxl2CJd\">here</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_HEkYKp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How easy is it to install the Revolve360?",
            "content": "<p>Installing the Revolve360 is easy with the Sure360 Safety Installation System, which includes a LockStrong belt tensioning arm to help you get a tight installation with either the lower anchor or the vehicle seat belt.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_EXwGf6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What is the definition of a LockStrong Arm?",
            "content": "<p>A LockStrong arm is a belt tensioning arm system that helps you easily achieve a tight installation with either the lower anchors (LATCH/UAS) or vehicle seat belt. It is built into the base and applies additional tension so you get a maximum result with minimal effort.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_Ec99LF": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Does the Revolve360 have a belt-tensioner or lock off?",
            "content": "<p>The LockStrong feature of the Revolve360 acts as a belt tensioner. Your vehicle seat belt MUST be locked to ensure accurate and safe installation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_yKLzFx": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What is the easiest way to install the Revolve360?",
            "content": "<p>The seat belt is the preferred method of installation for the Revolve360 because it allows you to take advantage of a true one-time installation. The tether should be used in both rear-facing and forward-facing harness installations, regardless of whether you have the car seat base installed with the seat belt or lower anchors (LATCH/UAS).</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_WrC9Rt": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What is the best way to install the Revolve360 if I plan to move it between cars?",
            "content": "<p>The seat belt is the preferred method of installation for the Revolve360 because it allows you to take advantage of a true one-time installation. The tether should be used in both rear-facing and forward-facing harness installations, regardless of whether you have the car seat base installed with the seat belt or lower anchors (LATCH/UAS).</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_hMQcGz": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What does one-time install mean?",
            "content": "<p>The one-time installation feature of the Revolve360 is really a differentiator. When used with the vehicle belt, you'll never have to re-install the car seat when used in rear- and forward-facing mode. (Note: the base needs to be reinstalled for belt positioning booster mode.)</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_gdRM6Q": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can the Revolve360 be reclined while installed?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. It's super easy to recline your rear-facing installation with the on-the-go recline feature. <em>(Keep in mind—the Revolve360 can only be reclined when in rear-facing mode.)</em></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3zYKfW": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Is the Revolve360 LATCH/UAS compatible?",
            "content": "<p>Yes.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_KwiPgM": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Up to what weight can you use LATCH?",
            "content": "<p>LATCH/UAS can be used up to 35 lb (15.9 kg) in Rear Facing and up to 40 lb (18 kg) in Forward Facing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_rwjPWy": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Is the tether required?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. The tether must be used when installing the Revolve360 in rear-facing or forward-facing harnessed mode. The tether is NOT used when using the Revolve360 in booster mode.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_k6md3Y": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can the Revolve360 b e tethered rear- and forward-facing?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, in fact the tether is required for use in both rear-facing and forward-facing harness modes.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_TPVyxk": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Where do I check to make sure I have a tight install?",
            "content": "<p>Firmly grip the car seat base near the belt path opening and try to move it side to side. The base should not move more than one inch (2.5 cm). If it moves more than one inch at the belt path, try your installation again. If it still moves more than one inch you may need to change seating positions in your vehicle or use a different installation method.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_cDN6La": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "I am installing the Revolve360 in rear-facing mode and I need the car seat to be more reclined. Can I use a rolled towel to increase the rear-facing recline?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, in certain situations. The Revolve 360 features four recline positions for rear-facing installations. The recline can be adjusted “on the fly” which means you are able to recline the child’s seating area after you have installed the car seat. There is a bead level on the side of the car seat which must be aligned with your child’s size. You may tightly roll a towel or use a section of pool noodle underneath the base of the car seat near the vehicle seat back to increase the recline angle, if necessary. The Revolve 360 can only be used in one recline position in forward-facing installations. You may NOT use a rolled towel or pool noodle to change the recline in forward-facing mode.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_6XYFMW": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Will this seat work in the middle seat of the car?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. The Revolve360 can be used in any forward-facing vehicle seating position allowed in your vehicle’s owner’s manual, as long as a tight installation can be achieved.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_U7krzE": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Will this car seat fit in my vehicle?",
            "content": "<p>There are many factors to consider when determining whether a specific car seat will fit in your vehicle. Your best option is to test the car seat in your vehicle before you make the purchase. It’s always worth asking for this option at your local retailer.</p><p>If you’re not able to try the car seat in your vehicle, we’ve provided some basic dimensions [in a table] below. Please note: the dimensions of your car seat and your vehicle’s back seat will not give you the full picture. There are many thousands of combinations of vehicle makes, models, car seat configurations, vehicle seat belt designs and seat cushion shapes. The easiest way to determine whether your car seat is suitable for a particular seating position is to check for a tight installation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_VDCCEQ": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "If I have both this car seat and a second car seat, will there be enough room to fit in a third passenger in my backseat?",
            "content": "<p>There are many combinations of vehicle makes, models, car seat configurations, vehicle seat belt designs and seat cushion shapes. The easiest way to determine whether your car seat is suitable for a particular seating position is to check for a tight installation, especially when trying to fit multiple passengers in the back seat of your vehicle.</p><p>Unfortunately, some smaller sedans and SUVs have rear seat belt systems that overlap, which makes it very difficult to fit three passengers in the rear seat.</p><p>In addition, the Revolve360 is designed to rotate allowing for easy loading and unloading for your child. The car seat will need some additional lateral space to accomplish the rotation, so fitting another car seat in the adjacent seating position may limit your use of that feature.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_yNnbJy": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Will I be able to fit three car seats in my back seat with the Revolve360?",
            "content": "<p>There are many thousands of combinations of vehicle makes, models, car seat configurations, vehicle seat belt designs and seat cushion shapes. The easiest way to determine whether your car seat is suitable for a particular seating position is to check for a tight installation, especially when trying to fit multiple passengers in the back seat of your vehicle.</p><p></p><p>The following conditions should be met when installing three car seats next to each other:<br/>- Each car seat must achieve a correct and tight installation.<br/>- The positions of the car seat on the vehicle seat are not changed by contact. Each car seat still aligns properly with respect to the seat belt or lower anchors that secure them and do not overlap the adjacent car seat.<br/>- If the vehicle seat is adjustable front-to-back, both portions of the vehicle seat must be adjusted to the same position.<br/>- Only one lower anchor connector is connected to a single lower anchor point.<br/>- There is no contact or force that would bend or deform any of the car seats.<br/>- The lower anchor belt or seat belt used to install each car seat does not rub on each other or crossover in a way that they interfere with each other.</p><p>In addition, the Revolve 360 is designed to rotate to make loading and unloading your child a breeze. The car seat will need some additional lateral space to accomplish the rotation, so fitting another car seat in the adjacent seating position may limit your use of that feature.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
