    "evenflo_faq_JLwM3L": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_R3nnyN": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "When removing the buckle from the Revolve360, does it matter if I pull the anchor out from the front or back slot?",
            "content": "<p>No. In order to use the Revolve 360 in belt positioning booster mode, you must remove the buckle from the car seat. Twist the bottom of the buckle so the strap lines up with the slot in the bottom of the car seat. Slide the strap while gently angling the metal anchor upwards. You can slide the buckle anchor out either the front or the back slot.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_XWCJrE": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do I remove the harness covers?",
            "content": "<p>Simply remove the tops of the harness covers for washing (just keep in mind that the lower part of the harness cover cannot be removed).</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_P7tnGe": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What is the purpose of the front flap on the seat pad?",
            "content": "<p>It provides padding to keep your little rider's legs comfy and flops out of the way for easy rotation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_nJeMrp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Does this seat fit taller kids?",
            "content": "<p>The Revolve360 was designed with a wide range of children in mind, from infants through big kids. Full product details are provided in the product instructions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_BjrWHV": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Is it okay for my child's feet to touch the vehicle seat back when in rear-facing mode?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. The Revolve360's extended seating area accommodates children in rear-facing mode until they are 40 inches (101 cm) tall or weigh-40 lbs (18 kg). The Revolve360’s anti-rebound surface is between your child and the vehicle seat. It's ok if their feet touch the surface.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_MEfTah": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "If using this seat in a second car or a caregiver's car, how easy is it to change modes for children of different ages?",
            "content": "<p>The Revolve360 makes switching the car seat between different children a breeze. The easy onetime installation allows you to rotate the seat between rear-facing and forward-facing modes without reinstalling the car seat. Additionally, the no-rethread harness can be raised or lowered by squeezing the handle at the top of the headrest – again, no need to reinstall the car seat!</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_eJVNTa": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I easily adjust the harness use to belt positioning booster use?",
            "content": "<p>The Revolve360 can be transitioned from harness to booster mode easily —simply follow the included User Guide or our booster installation video.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
