    "evenflo_faq_GWRbpR": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_da7aML": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can the car seat be used without cup holders?",
            "content": "<p>Yes you can use this product without the cup holders attached to the car seat. The Revolve360 is all about flexibility and convenience. The cup holders are even safe to be placed in the top rack of your dishwasher for cleaning.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_EkmCbL": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I purchase an extra base?",
            "content": "<p>No, not at this time.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_MUHW8T": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I use the Revolve360 without the base?",
            "content": "<p>No – the car seat must be used with the base.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_UXk8n4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do I know the car seat is locked into place?",
            "content": "<p>The Red/Green Seat Lock Indicator is a fast, easy way to make sure the Revolve360 is locked into place. The indicator will turn green when the seat is locked in a rear-facing or forward-facing position. The indicator must show green when the child is in the car seat for travel in the vehicle.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_eeWqrw": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Will the Revolve360 rotate on its own?",
            "content": "<p>No. In the interest of safety, only the parent/caregiver can rotate the car seat by squeezing the rotation handle on either side of the car seat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_pUhEHt": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Since this seat rotates, how do I know it won't rotate on its own?",
            "content": "<p>You'll find indicators on either side of the base allowing you to easily check the seat's Locked/Unlocked status.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_WhWPpb": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Does the Revolve360 move when the car is in motion because of the rotational feature?",
            "content": "<p>No. The Revolve360 is designed to be safe and secure when you're on-the-go. There are Seat Lock indicators on either side of the base that must be green while your child is traveling in the car seat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_7mQnp7": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can another child (sitting next to the seat) reach over to the Revolve360 to make it rotate while I'm driving?",
            "content": "<p>No, rest easy. The Revolve360 has you covered on safety from all angles. Only the parent/caregiver can rotate the car seat by squeezing the rotation handle on either side of the car seat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_rVbHUh": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Do the rotational components wear over time?",
            "content": "<p>Remember — this is an extended use car seat that's designed to take you from babyhood to ten years-old. The product has been tested to meet strict cycling and durability standards, so it's built to take you through childhood.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_dpigFi": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can the Revolve360 use any other style LATCH/UAS?",
            "content": "<p>The Revolve360 should only be used with the LATCH/UAS that is included with your purchase.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_6ELWge": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "I tried to rotate my Evenflo Gold Revolve360, but my seat got stuck and will not move in any direction now. What do I do?",
            "content": "<p>First, squeeze the recline adjustment handle (located behind the car seat) and adjust the car seat into the fully-reclined position – even if you plan to rotate the seat for forward-facing use. If you are having difficulty reclining the car seat, try the following: squeeze the recline adjustment handle, pull up slightly on the back of the car seat and then push down quickly and firmly on the car seat back.</p><p>Once the car seat is in the fully-reclined position, squeeze the rotation handle and rotate the car seat to either the rear-facing or forward-facing position.</p><p>Please note that the fully-reclined position becomes the fully-upright position as you rotate the car seat into the forward-facing position.</p><p>If you still are unable to get the car seat to recline or rotate, please contact ParentLink at 1-800-233-5921 (U.S.) or 1-937-773-3971 (Canada), Monday – Friday, 8 am – 5 pm (EST).</p>"
          }
        }
      },
