    "evenflo_faq_hfgXqL": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_JiPeHr": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "If car seats are required by government regulation to be flame-retardant, how does Evenflo make sure it meets the government standard?",
            "content": "<p>Flammability testing of car seats is required under the FMVSS 302, Flammability of Interior Materials Standard. The test measures the rate of flame spread with the goal of maximizing the amount of time a caregiver would have to remove an occupant from the car seat in the event of a vehicle fire. Evenflo’s car seats are tested by an accredited independent testing laboratory and meet the FMVSS 302 standard.</p><p>In addition, Evenflo car seats are tested for toxicity to meet or exceed the requirements of various state and federal child products banned substances laws and regulations.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_zmkThm": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Does the black fabric get hot in the summer?",
            "content": "<p>Like all black fabrics, the black fabric on your car seat will get warmer the longer the seat is exposed to sunlight. In warmer months, you can place a towel or sheet over the car seat when it is not in use to help keep it cool.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_kg6FLa": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How comfortable are the fabrics for my baby?",
            "content": "<p>The Evenflo Gold Revolve360 is designed with premium, soft fabrics that have a smooth finish for easy spot cleaning. Your baby will love the plush feel.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
